<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>MMCA.Common.AI.Testing</PackageId>
    <Description>MMCA framework evaluation harness for the governed language-model boundary: a replay IChatClient over recorded Microsoft.Extensions.AI responses, abstract xUnit bases for a golden-replay gate and for pinning every PromptContract to a recorded hash, so a prompt change cannot ship unevaluated and a corpus survives a provider swap</Description>
    <!--
      This package ships abstract xUnit [Fact] bases, so it carries test-style member names
      (underscores). Relax the documentation analyzers exactly as the sibling
      MMCA.Common.Testing.Architecture package does for test infrastructure, plus CA1707 (underscores
      in the inherited [Fact] method names) and only the rules the code still triggers (kept minimal
      on purpose). S2699 ("add at least one assertion") goes with them: these [Fact] bodies report a
      violation by throwing with the full list of what failed, which is the assertion, and the rule
      only recognizes a call into an assertion library.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1707;S2699;SA1600;SA1601;SA1602;SA1611;SA1615;SA1618;SA1623;SA1629;SA1642;SA1649;MA0076;MA0127;RCS1112</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MinVer">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>build</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3.extensibility.core" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    The governed package and nothing else. A vendor SDK reference here would defeat the point: the
    corpus is recorded in the Microsoft.Extensions.AI shape, so the same recorded answers replay
    unchanged after a provider swap. The harness needs PromptContract (the hash a recorded corpus is
    keyed on) and the Microsoft.Extensions.AI abstractions it arrives with, so it takes the AI
    package by project reference and stays free of every other MMCA layer
    (EnforceAiLayerBoundary in MMCA.Common.LayerEnforcement.targets matches this project too, by the
    MMCA.Common.AI. prefix).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\MMCA.Common.AI\MMCA.Common.AI.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
